@startuml
title syncweatherstations-cron local architecture

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 220

actor "Cron scheduler" as Cron

package "Spin app\napps/syncweatherstations-cron" {
  component "Cron handler\nsrc/lib.rs" as CronHandler
  component "Composed component\ncomposed.wasm" as Composed
  component "Adapter\nadapter/src/lib.rs" as Adapter
  component "Sync engine\ncomponents/syncweatherstations" as SyncEngine
}

package "Compose sidecars" {
  component "dmi-proxy\nnginx reverse proxy" as DmiProxy
  database "weatherstations-db\nPostgreSQL 18" as Db
  component "otel-collector" as OTel
  component "jaeger" as Jaeger
}

cloud "External services" {
  component "DMI station API" as DmiApi
}

Cron --> CronHandler : cron tick
CronHandler --> Composed : invoke runner.sync()
Composed --> SyncEngine : composed guest call
SyncEngine --> Adapter : transport.get(url)\nstorage.persist(stations)

Adapter --> DmiProxy : HTTP GET /v2/metObs/collections/station/items
DmiProxy --> DmiApi : HTTPS GET to DMI

Adapter --> Db : migration + advisory lock + upserts

CronHandler ..> OTel : logs and traces
Adapter ..> OTel : HTTP / DB spans
OTel --> Jaeger : export traces

note right of SyncEngine
Validates trusted DMI URLs,
deduplicates features,
and builds the sync summary.
end note

note bottom of Adapter
If dmi_proxy_base_url is set,
the adapter rewrites the outbound
DMI fetch to the local proxy while
preserving path and query.
end note

@enduml
